## Scope and coverage

This curriculum is a labelled validation artifact, not an active course plan or learner record. The lesson reasoning/keys are ready for a contract check; production readiness remains false until ingest issues an actual course revision and plan commits in the real course record directory. The validation-local revision is provenance, not a fabricated production state.

| Requested capability | Finished note location | Objectives | Coverage |
|---|---|---|---|
| Explain specific sunk investment, bargaining and before/after incentives | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#2. Hold-up: investment changes bargaining power|Hold-up]] | O001 | bounded complete |
| Distinguish pure sequential commitment and hidden information | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#3. Commitment: promises can become unattractive to keep|Commitment]] and [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#1. Information: hidden quality and hidden action|Information]] | O001 | only contrast needed for hold-up |
| Calculate/interpret project versus operating outcomes and thresholds | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#2. Hold-up: investment changes bargaining power|Corrected axle illustration]] | O002 | bounded complete |

Completion provenance: [complete ingestion pass](../../runtime/ingest/logs/20261003T142217+0200_behavioral_week1.md). Source identities and semantic baseline: [manifest](source_manifest.md). The pass's final course is Comparative Economics despite its original folder/run name.

Uncovered: other transaction problems beyond the contrasts; full formal/informal institutions curriculum; developmental causal evidence; other Week 1 notes; whole syllabus/exam; valuation, uncertainty, alternative-buyer/salvage calculations. No unsupported dependency is hidden. The adjacent mechanism contrasts are introduced before mixed assessment. No exam-coverage claim is made.

## Teaching sequence

| Order | Objective/block | Necessary prerequisite + reason | Entry | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [O001 outcome](lessons/O001.md#outcome-and-conditions) | Local sunk-cost/outside-option foundation taught in block; mechanism depends on timing/specificity | P1 then explanation/example/F1/I1/I2 | curriculum ready |
| 2 | [O002 outcome](lessons/O002.md#outcome-and-conditions) | O001 timing distinction prevents confusing total accounting with the current comparison; per-unit arithmetic checked by P1 | P1 then derivation/W1/F1/I1/I2 | curriculum ready |

Order: identify the mechanism without arithmetic first, then quantify the two distinct decisions. The procedure remains a meaningful capability separate from verbal recognition; neither substitutes for the other. Adequate compatible evidence can skip redundant support according to lesson checks; this artifact contains none. Small blocks permit targeted retrieval of explanation, key/rubric or correction without loading the full course.

## Execution and assessment contract

Each lesson supplies motivation, intuition, definitions/conditions, intermediate steps, worked example, supported practice, independent practice, keys, rubric, fresh correction, delayed variants and escalation rules. O001 requires independent mechanism (including remedy plus limitation) and discrimination roles; O002 requires calculation and interpretation roles. Normally two distinct current-criterion passes qualify acquisition. Delayed checks separately require 24 actual hours, fresh tasks and known independent conditions. These are pragmatic auditable defaults, not proven personal optima.

Review titles/instructions in metadata contain no answers or dates. Teach records actual evidence; recall alone schedules and synchronizes tasks. Conceptual, procedural and interpretive results remain component-specific. One immediate pass is not durable mastery.

## Revisions and evidence compatibility

P001/V001 established O001 revision 1/O001-C1 and O002 revision 1/O002-C1. P002/V001 adds the explicit compatibility field and committed-journal verification contract only; learning outcome, question and rubric definitions are unchanged. Exact P001 files are retained under [immutable curriculum history](curriculum_history/P001/learning_plan.md). No learner evidence is mapped or fabricated; compatibility lists remain empty because this artifact has no learner history. P003/V001 preserves the exact P002 bundle under [P002 history](curriculum_history/P002/learning_plan.md), keeps stable IDs/objective outcomes/revisions, and increments O001 criterion to O001-C2. Its alternate mechanism prompts/keys now explicitly assess the required remedy and limitation; old O001-C1 success is not sufficient for this criterion. Gate G-O001-C2 requires the full current acquisition roles with fresh independent items; no historic result is regraded. O002-C1 is unchanged. No previous objective definitions/evidence are migrated or reinterpreted. No synthetic evidence is entered into course history. If a later version changes thresholds/conditions/criteria, preserve this complete version under immutable curriculum history, increment affected versions and prepare reassessment; unchanged formatting can retain compatibility with an explicit reason.

## Validation and readiness

See [rehearsal](REHEARSAL.md) for first-learning, incorrect-answer correction and delayed-review contract traces. A stdlib check verifies metadata tuple, note hash/heading targets, mandatory lesson sections, dependency acyclicity and every prepared numeric key. A committed validation-only transaction stages plan/manifest/lessons with matching tuple. No faster-model performance, learner outcome, real Todoist operation or full exam coverage is claimed.
